      "description": "Five people were killed and more than a dozen injured after a gunman opened fire Saturday afternoon in a market square in Krakow, Poland, police said.\nThe gunman aimed at random people as he drove by the city's Main Square, Krakow police said. Police officers are among the wounded.\nThe perpetrator was shot and wounded during a confrontation with police.\nPolish Prime Minister Donald Tusk, in a post on X, said police are investigating the attack.\nOther details were not immediately available.\nKrakow is the second-largest city in Poland and roughly 250 kilometres from the capital, Warsaw.",
